uuid "2afdaff0-fd03-5d5a-9b50-c71e5077877b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315370} {:answer/id #uuid "48a43274-16a8-55d9-a83a-9deaa58b42c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315537} {:answer/id #uuid "8e7619dc-5aff-5054-8800-bb71d5b9826a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315916} {:answer/id #uuid "cc610ca7-4121-59bb-8b6e-2e667e4b319e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316276} {:answer/id #uuid "f24b10d1-1646-5236-ba37-c6e42ab5dac6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316469} {:answer/id #uuid "f3430536-0938-5bab-b667-c39bdaac5375" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "piecewise continuous" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316476} {:answer/id #uuid "f8779403-3b1c-590e-a881-326314ab16ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316506}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f3430536-0938-5bab-b667-c39bdaac5375" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "piecewise continuous" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316476} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8cf181a-e3d2-5269-b318-b692a92a9f47" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316983}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "01fa87ea-c90a-5da0-b692-1e4e4dbca851" :question/math-academy-id "q-343339" :question/problem "Let $f(x)$ be the $2$-periodic extension of the function $F(x)=-4x$ defined on $[-1,1).$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below, showing the derivation of a series converging to the $2$-periodic extension of \n\n$$\nG(x)=-2{x}^{2}={\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nfrom the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x).$The Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n-4x∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{8(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }{{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nSince $f$ is \n{{field-2}} \non $R,$ we may integrate its Fourier series term-by-term to get\n\n$$\n-2{x}^{2}∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{{field-3}}\\cdot {{field-4}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $F(x)$ is an odd function. So, the Fourier series of its $2L$-periodic extension has the form\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{L}).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=1$ and we are already given the coefficients ${b}_{n}$ for $n\\ge 1.$ Thus, the Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{8(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi x).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the function $F$ is continuous on $(-1,1).$ \nTherefore, the $2$-periodic extension $f$ is $\\text{piecewise continuous}$ on $R,$ so we may integrate its Fourier series term-by-term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}(-4t)\\,\\text{d}t & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{8(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ [-2{t}^{2}]_{0}^{x} & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{8(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }\\cdot [-\\frac{1}{n\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi t)]_{0}^{x} \\\\ -2{x}^{2} & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,\\frac{8(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\cdot (1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x))\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
